1
00:00:13,511 --> 00:00:15,081
Ravi!

2
00:00:28,917 --> 00:00:31,676
No, no, no...

3
00:00:35,930 --> 00:00:37,357
Ravi!

4
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:11,067
Excuse me.

5
00:01:15,355 --> 00:01:18,621
Where will I find Shekhar Home?

6
00:01:20,714 --> 00:01:21,754
Shekhar?

7
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:23,380
Shekhar?

8
00:01:24,644 --> 00:01:26,844
-What?
-There is a girl here to see you.

9
00:01:35,472 --> 00:01:38,019
They are behaving like they're
seeing a girl for the first time

10
00:01:38,749 --> 00:01:40,189
like in a boys hostel.

11
00:01:41,355 --> 00:01:43,815
Maybe they're seeing a
girl with you for the first time?

12
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:48,680
Oh, that...

13
00:01:51,019 --> 00:01:52,059
is the just the way I am.

14
00:01:53,527 --> 00:01:54,567
Alone...

15
00:01:55,089 --> 00:01:56,089
and happy.

16
00:01:56,152 --> 00:01:57,152
Should I leave?

17
00:01:57,613 --> 00:01:59,683
Where? Oh no, I just...

18
00:02:00,738 --> 00:02:01,738
What?

19
00:02:02,293 --> 00:02:03,333
Oh, I see.

20
00:02:05,441 --> 00:02:07,315
So you're using emotional
blackmail this time.

21
00:02:09,441 --> 00:02:10,691
More interesting than that.

22
00:02:13,214 --> 00:02:14,839
I have a case for you this time.

23
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:19,738
Do you believe in ghosts?

24
00:02:23,285 --> 00:02:24,363
I... I don't mind

25
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:54,320
DAATGUNJ

26
00:03:03,303 --> 00:03:04,383
Aunt Reena...

27
00:03:11,143 --> 00:03:12,777
-Hemant?
-Yeah.

28
00:03:15,613 --> 00:03:17,496
Mr. Home, Mr. Saini.

29
00:03:18,613 --> 00:03:19,653
Thank you for coming.

30
00:03:20,144 --> 00:03:23,160
I am Hemant and this is
my dad Sanjeev Bhaskar.

31
00:03:24,011 --> 00:03:25,168
Sorry for your loss.

32
00:03:27,214 --> 00:03:28,300
Who is that lady?

33
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:32,918
Kakoli.

34
00:03:33,121 --> 00:03:35,074
She calls herself a tantrik(witch doctor)
but she is a fraud.

35
00:03:36,261 --> 00:03:39,332
She opens shop every time
there is an unusual death.

36
00:03:43,011 --> 00:03:44,019
What's Kakoli?

37
00:04:03,261 --> 00:04:05,863
He won't spare anyone!

38
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:09,121
He won't spare anyone.

39
00:04:09,441 --> 00:04:11,863
You will all die...

40
00:04:13,238 --> 00:04:14,613
You will die.

41
00:04:16,378 --> 00:04:20,628
You will die too man, you will.

42
00:04:28,824 --> 00:04:29,957
You will die too.

43
00:04:30,707 --> 00:04:33,113
You will all die!

44
00:04:33,496 --> 00:04:36,246
He won't spare anyone.
Everyone will die.

45
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:40,324
-Everyone will die...
-Hey get lost! Get out of here!

46
00:04:40,535 --> 00:04:43,082
He won't spare anyone.

47
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:47,070
BHASKAR VILLA

48
00:04:55,988 --> 00:04:57,028
Please.

49
00:05:01,355 --> 00:05:02,355
Wow...

50
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:07,283
This place looks
like a sofa showroom.

51
00:05:07,490 --> 00:05:08,563
Really big.

52
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:11,543
This is your first
visit to Bhaskar Villa

53
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,393
and on such a terrible occasion...

54
00:05:13,472 --> 00:05:15,300
The guy who died...

55
00:05:15,722 --> 00:05:17,150
I mean, passed away...

56
00:05:17,191 --> 00:05:18,523
How was he related to you?

57
00:05:18,714 --> 00:05:20,839
Ravi uncle. My dad's younger brother.

58
00:05:22,777 --> 00:05:24,824
Sarita aunty. Ravi uncle's wife.

59
00:05:25,574 --> 00:05:27,011
His daughter Pakhi and

60
00:05:27,847 --> 00:05:28,847
Aunt Reena.

61
00:05:30,964 --> 00:05:31,964
Nice painting.

62
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:34,066
Very lifelike.

63
00:05:34,558 --> 00:05:37,480
It feels like they are going
to come out and say hello.

64
00:05:41,699 --> 00:05:43,011
Sorry...

65
00:05:45,207 --> 00:05:47,285
So you guys aren't
originally from here, right?

66
00:05:48,402 --> 00:05:50,428
Actually we have been
here for eight generations.

67
00:05:51,748 --> 00:05:53,027
We are originally from Bilaspur.

68
00:05:54,793 --> 00:05:55,996
We were coal merchants

69
00:05:56,663 --> 00:05:59,928
who would take coal from Dhanbad and
sell it to the East India Company.

70
00:06:00,999 --> 00:06:03,655
Since then the whole
family has always lived here.

71
00:06:03,952 --> 00:06:05,072
So Ravi...

72
00:06:05,335 --> 00:06:07,241
Why are you all standing? Please sit.

73
00:06:07,725 --> 00:06:09,444
Make yourselves at home. Sit.

74
00:06:11,133 --> 00:06:12,133
Please sit.

75
00:06:13,616 --> 00:06:15,905
Sit Ms. Sarita, Pakhi...

76
00:06:16,383 --> 00:06:17,383
Aunt Reena,

77
00:06:17,968 --> 00:06:20,608
Sanjeev Bhaskar, how
did Ravi Bhaskar die?

78
00:06:21,835 --> 00:06:25,030
Actually, two days ago
when we were having dinner...

79
00:06:26,139 --> 00:06:28,694
everything was normal,
the mood was jovial,

80
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:34,085
and then Ravi uncle got
up to go to the washroom.

81
00:06:36,796 --> 00:06:38,218
He was gone for 5 minutes

82
00:06:39,507 --> 00:06:43,123
but when he came back
his behaviour was a bit...

83
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,760
weird.

84
00:06:44,796 --> 00:06:46,163
What kind of behaviour?

85
00:06:46,617 --> 00:06:49,203
Do you wear sarees or
do you not get the chance?

86
00:06:49,553 --> 00:06:50,718
Dad, are you okay?

87
00:06:53,889 --> 00:06:54,889
Ravi?

88
00:06:55,757 --> 00:06:56,757
Are you okay?

89
00:06:57,561 --> 00:06:59,327
He would have a drink every evening,

90
00:06:59,725 --> 00:07:03,256
maybe he had a bit
too much that night?

91
00:07:03,686 --> 00:07:04,686
I see.

92
00:07:05,061 --> 00:07:09,210
And that same night Aunt Reena
heard something in the hall and

93
00:07:09,405 --> 00:07:11,975
when she stepped out
of her room to check...

94
00:07:12,991 --> 00:07:15,405
It looked like Ravi was running
away from something in fear.

95
00:07:18,585 --> 00:07:20,257
When I saw him it looked like...

96
00:07:21,311 --> 00:07:23,076
he might have seen him.

97
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:25,053
Um... Him who?

98
00:07:25,374 --> 00:07:26,968
You know... him!

99
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,440
Sorry?

100
00:07:30,468 --> 00:07:31,468
Skawndhokaata.

101
00:07:31,913 --> 00:07:32,913
Did what?

102
00:07:33,507 --> 00:07:34,547
Skawndhokaata.

103
00:07:35,983 --> 00:07:37,655
Once he gets a hold of someone,

104
00:07:37,952 --> 00:07:40,374
that person goes crazy.

105
00:07:40,883 --> 00:07:42,449
And that craziness...

106
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:44,503
could drive someone
to kill themselves.

107
00:07:44,874 --> 00:07:47,074
God knows how many such incidents
took place over the last 150 years--

108
00:07:47,115 --> 00:07:49,400
This is why you're here.

109
00:07:49,425 --> 00:07:51,670
This bullshit Skawndhokaata story.

110
00:07:51,850 --> 00:07:53,963
You know the air, water and soil

111
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:56,440
in Daatgunj are mixed
with fear and superstition.

112
00:07:56,538 --> 00:07:59,284
They say that someone
was sacrificed a long time ago

113
00:07:59,424 --> 00:08:01,983
and his headless ghost
now wanders around.

114
00:08:02,350 --> 00:08:06,604
And then every abnormal death
is blamed on Skawndhokaata.

115
00:08:06,628 --> 00:08:08,405
Which is... Which is ridiculous!

116
00:08:09,014 --> 00:08:11,299
And now my whole family thinks

117
00:08:11,323 --> 00:08:14,436
that Ravi uncle was killed
by this Skawndhokaata.

118
00:08:14,573 --> 00:08:16,131
Do you think I am lying?

119
00:08:16,718 --> 00:08:19,202
Aunty... I didn't blame you...

120
00:08:20,874 --> 00:08:24,733
Mr. Home, my uncle was
not killed by Skawndhokaata.

121
00:08:25,678 --> 00:08:27,842
Please prove this to my family,
that's all I want.

122
00:08:29,889 --> 00:08:33,037
An investigation cannot end
a 150-year-old superstition.

123
00:08:36,077 --> 00:08:37,117
We appreciate you coming

124
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:40,560
because Hemant got another
chance to say what he wanted.

125
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:42,811
I am sure you must be tired.

126
00:08:44,468 --> 00:08:45,468
Please rest here.

127
00:08:46,663 --> 00:08:48,240
Then you can leave tomorrow.

128
00:08:50,061 --> 00:08:51,367
Why wait till tomorrow?

129
00:08:52,046 --> 00:08:55,186
We are ready to go back today.

130
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:59,170
You just need to show
us his post-mortem report--

131
00:08:59,202 --> 00:09:00,795
Look, we don't do that here.

132
00:09:01,882 --> 00:09:02,882
Hemant,

133
00:09:03,288 --> 00:09:04,483
stop this nonsense.

134
00:09:05,702 --> 00:09:06,858
Sanjeev uncle,

135
00:09:07,702 --> 00:09:09,046
now that they are here

136
00:09:09,530 --> 00:09:10,870
let them conduct an investigation.

137
00:09:10,894 --> 00:09:12,319
Yes, please. Thank you.

138
00:09:14,108 --> 00:09:15,108
Please?

139
00:09:18,436 --> 00:09:20,225
So where is the dining room?
Should we go?

140
00:09:24,144 --> 00:09:25,199
Who is this?

141
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,053
This is Manoj, our Estate Manager.

142
00:09:28,327 --> 00:09:29,393
Please.

143
00:09:29,474 --> 00:09:30,487
He is very young.

144
00:09:33,655 --> 00:09:34,535
Give it to brother.

145
00:09:51,210 --> 00:09:53,718
Ravi uncle just kept
walking into the water

146
00:09:54,671 --> 00:09:55,811
and then he drowned himself.

147
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,663
How do you know these people?

148
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:09,108
Sanjeev uncle and
Hemant invested in my NGO,

149
00:10:09,546 --> 00:10:11,913
we met because of that and
then we became friends.

150
00:10:12,343 --> 00:10:13,663
And Ravi uncle who passed away?

151
00:10:14,421 --> 00:10:16,225
Ravi uncle's whole family
lived in the US.

152
00:10:17,827 --> 00:10:19,347
This was his first
visit in five years.

153
00:10:20,288 --> 00:10:21,538
And then all of this happened.

154
00:10:24,616 --> 00:10:26,296
And what about...

155
00:10:26,403 --> 00:10:28,490
I am sorry for asking
so many questions.

156
00:10:30,085 --> 00:10:31,085
Aunt Reena?

157
00:10:32,077 --> 00:10:34,237
Aunt Reena is like
a mother to Hemant.

158
00:10:35,194 --> 00:10:37,255
After Hemant's
mother passed away...

159
00:10:37,302 --> 00:10:38,411
she never married.

160
00:10:38,749 --> 00:10:40,897
She was the one who raised Hemant.

161
00:10:41,663 --> 00:10:42,983
They're quite a lovely family.

162
00:10:43,725 --> 00:10:45,330
They have given me a lot of love.

163
00:10:46,053 --> 00:10:47,702
I have even performed
in this garden.

164
00:10:47,983 --> 00:10:48,983
Oh.

165
00:10:49,085 --> 00:10:50,475
Sanjeev uncle loves music

166
00:10:51,171 --> 00:10:52,272
and Hemant is the opposite.

167
00:10:52,858 --> 00:10:54,210
That's just how they are.

168
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,871
Hemant doesn't like music at all.

169
00:10:56,978 --> 00:10:58,431
And musicians?

170
00:11:00,218 --> 00:11:01,382
No... I...

171
00:11:01,796 --> 00:11:03,262
Musicians...

172
00:11:03,396 --> 00:11:05,703
only like other musicians.

173
00:11:13,593 --> 00:11:16,256
The only thing Hemant is
passionate about is his plants.

174
00:11:17,405 --> 00:11:18,666
He is a botany enthusiast.

175
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:22,233
He can spend hours
talking about his plants.

176
00:11:23,178 --> 00:11:24,178
I can see...

177
00:11:25,678 --> 00:11:26,718
the enthusiasm.

178
00:11:37,678 --> 00:11:39,611
What could be so scary, Mr. Home,

179
00:11:39,652 --> 00:11:44,615
that a man woke up and walked
into the pond to commit suicide?

180
00:11:49,827 --> 00:11:53,835
Have you noticed the somber
mood of the whole village?

181
00:11:55,363 --> 00:11:57,018
Let's find out partner.

182
00:11:58,694 --> 00:12:01,952
Iraboty, let's go
meet the villagers.

183
00:12:02,030 --> 00:12:03,678
Why? Why do you want to meet them?

184
00:12:04,008 --> 00:12:06,187
-To find out more about Skawndhokaata--
-Skawndhokaata.

185
00:12:06,228 --> 00:12:07,921
Again, this is why I told you.

186
00:12:09,382 --> 00:12:11,875
The villagers believe that
talking about Skawndhokaata

187
00:12:11,916 --> 00:12:13,802
is as good as inviting him.

188
00:12:14,444 --> 00:12:15,797
Stay away from the villagers.

189
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,840
Do not insult their
beliefs and feelings.

190
00:12:22,952 --> 00:12:23,992
Good morning.

191
00:12:33,132 --> 00:12:35,532
Hi... have you seen Skawndhokaata?

192
00:12:35,573 --> 00:12:37,152
The guy whose head was cut off?

193
00:12:38,397 --> 00:12:40,583
You know Skawndhokaata?
=The one without...

194
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:41,950
Who didn't have...

195
00:12:42,311 --> 00:12:43,703
Hey! Stop!

196
00:12:43,728 --> 00:12:44,770
Uncle!

197
00:12:51,788 --> 00:12:53,436
-Come with me.
-What?

198
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:55,157
Come with me.

199
00:15:03,882 --> 00:15:05,397
Biren!

200
00:15:58,663 --> 00:15:59,780
Shekhar?

201
00:16:00,858 --> 00:16:03,288
Isn't that the guy who
said we would all die?

202
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,912
Sir, why aren't you taking the body

203
00:16:19,632 --> 00:16:21,792
for post-mortem instead of this
superstitious nonsense?

204
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:23,616
This is the Daatgunj way.

205
00:16:24,319 --> 00:16:26,147
These villagers won't
let me move the body.

206
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:28,311
Along with Skawndhokaata's prey.

207
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:31,036
How do you know that Skawndhokaata
was the one who killed him?

208
00:16:31,089 --> 00:16:32,498
Hey Mahto, come here.

209
00:16:33,882 --> 00:16:35,116
Tell him what you told me.

210
00:16:44,913 --> 00:16:46,643
What are you doing sir?
You're wasting time!

211
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:47,940
You again?

212
00:16:47,975 --> 00:16:49,015
Hey, lock this guy up.

213
00:16:49,616 --> 00:16:50,710
Your police station...

214
00:16:52,585 --> 00:16:54,835
comes under DIG
sengupta's jurisdiction, right?

215
00:16:55,569 --> 00:16:57,584
-Yes.
-Do you want to hear it from him?

216
00:16:59,647 --> 00:17:00,647
What?

217
00:17:01,475 --> 00:17:05,556
Brother, why do you want to involve
the DIG in such a small case?

218
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:06,800
Please forget about it.

219
00:17:06,819 --> 00:17:09,218
I will. Bring him down first.

220
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,515
It will be a big problem brother.

221
00:17:11,812 --> 00:17:14,140
You are not from around here,
you can just leave.

222
00:17:14,413 --> 00:17:15,429
We have to live here.

223
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,500
Is this how you fulfill your
duty even though you live here?

224
00:17:29,819 --> 00:17:31,259
You don't know what you are doing.

225
00:17:31,858 --> 00:17:34,366
And what are the
rest of you staring at?

226
00:17:35,116 --> 00:17:36,656
He might be the one
committing the sin

227
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:37,915
but we will all have
to pay the price.

228
00:17:37,956 --> 00:17:39,489
It will be a disaster!

229
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:42,920
Do something! Stop them!

230
00:17:43,851 --> 00:17:47,316
Hey! Hurry up and remove
the body before they come back.

231
00:17:47,648 --> 00:17:50,819
Come on hurry up. Move it.

232
00:17:52,132 --> 00:17:53,905
Come on, let's go.

233
00:17:54,148 --> 00:17:56,186
Hey wait! Go after them.

234
00:17:57,023 --> 00:17:58,569
Run! Catch them!

235
00:17:58,610 --> 00:18:00,136
-Run!
-That's what I am doing.

236
00:18:00,507 --> 00:18:03,593
-This Iraboty will get us killed!
-They're throwing rocks, careful!

237
00:18:03,858 --> 00:18:06,351
Forget about Skawndhokaata,
these villagers will kill us.

238
00:18:11,366 --> 00:18:13,452
Go, go, go!

239
00:18:20,663 --> 00:18:22,648
This Iraboty has made you go crazy,

240
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:25,280
why don't you choose safe
and high-paying jobs?

241
00:18:25,655 --> 00:18:27,757
Go tell her. She is right there.

242
00:18:29,842 --> 00:18:30,842
They're here.

243
00:18:31,476 --> 00:18:33,171
How could you be so stupid?

244
00:18:33,491 --> 00:18:35,569
-What now?
-Did you even think this through?

245
00:18:35,976 --> 00:18:38,796
And you guys, are you happy now?

246
00:18:39,358 --> 00:18:40,798
Now that the whole village is angry.

247
00:18:41,226 --> 00:18:42,866
They can come all
the way to our home!

248
00:18:43,015 --> 00:18:45,960
Brother's BP is rising.
What if he falls sick?

249
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:47,203
I will talk to them Aunty.

250
00:18:47,351 --> 00:18:49,155
Ms. Reena, don't mind but

251
00:18:49,437 --> 00:18:52,343
we are putting our lives in
danger to investigate this case

252
00:18:52,384 --> 00:18:53,617
because Iraboty asked us to.

253
00:18:53,866 --> 00:18:56,592
And this is the first time that
a victim of Skawndhokaata's

254
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:57,960
will get a post-mortem.

255
00:18:58,569 --> 00:19:01,265
I think that's progress, you know?

256
00:19:01,437 --> 00:19:04,421
Do me a favour and
don't leave this house!

257
00:19:04,562 --> 00:19:06,687
Stay at home, that
is best for everyone.

258
00:19:06,976 --> 00:19:08,183
And especially you!

259
00:19:08,237 --> 00:19:09,690
Can I... freshen up?

260
00:19:09,812 --> 00:19:11,413
Yes, please go.

261
00:19:13,898 --> 00:19:15,163
You are unbelievable!

262
00:20:30,093 --> 00:20:31,733
Shekhar!

263
00:21:11,413 --> 00:21:12,976
Shekhar!

264
00:21:51,335 --> 00:21:54,831
Shekhar! No Shekhar! Shekhar stop!

265
00:21:54,855 --> 00:22:00,428
No Shekhar! Stop it!

266
00:22:06,967 --> 00:22:08,640
Have you come to
your senses, Partner?

267
00:22:19,046 --> 00:22:20,390
Good morning.

268
00:22:20,490 --> 00:22:21,570
Good morning.

269
00:22:21,874 --> 00:22:23,937
Say "Thank you"
instead of "Good morning"

270
00:22:24,663 --> 00:22:27,960
If I hadn't saved you last
night you would be dead.

271
00:22:28,530 --> 00:22:30,312
I am sorry I got you into all this.

272
00:22:31,499 --> 00:22:32,733
What happened last night?

273
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:38,160
Skawndhokaata.

274
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,083
Skawndhokaata?

275
00:22:45,327 --> 00:22:46,367
It's real.

276
00:22:47,023 --> 00:22:48,063
What?

277
00:22:49,499 --> 00:22:50,804
Come on Shekhar...

278
00:22:56,069 --> 00:22:57,858
Skawndhokaata is real.

279
00:23:00,054 --> 00:23:01,804
We need to go back
to Biren's house.

280
00:23:04,179 --> 00:23:05,780
But if Skawndhokaata is there,

281
00:23:05,804 --> 00:23:08,374
then why are you talking
about going back there?

282
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:10,937
Because I won't go alone this time.

283
00:23:10,999 --> 00:23:12,892
Will you take the army
and the police with you?

284
00:23:13,288 --> 00:23:14,866
No that will take too long.

285
00:23:15,999 --> 00:23:17,405
We will all go.

286
00:23:19,179 --> 00:23:21,099
Carry a handkerchief
because that place stinks.

287
00:23:52,526 --> 00:23:55,433
What were you doing outside
Biren's house last night?

288
00:23:57,503 --> 00:23:59,019
Me? Not at all...

289
00:24:06,401 --> 00:24:08,128
What do you know about Kakoli?

290
00:24:10,034 --> 00:24:11,870
The same as everyone else.

291
00:24:12,714 --> 00:24:14,587
She is a witch doctor
who reads horoscopes

292
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:16,560
and makes predictions, that's all.

293
00:24:16,839 --> 00:24:19,792
But everyone knows that,
what do you know?

294
00:24:20,972 --> 00:24:23,456
She is your good friend, right?

295
00:24:30,565 --> 00:24:33,675
Why don't you show
me proof of that...

296
00:24:33,714 --> 00:24:37,604
Ms. Reena I have a
lie detector in my head.

297
00:24:38,511 --> 00:24:40,277
Whenever someone
lies the alarm rings.

298
00:24:40,318 --> 00:24:41,591
It's very irritating.

299
00:25:08,909 --> 00:25:10,120
I don't see Kakoli anywhere.

300
00:25:17,964 --> 00:25:19,004
What are you looking for?

301
00:25:23,276 --> 00:25:24,356
Let's look somewhere else.

302
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,527
Hey Kakoli!

303
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:42,846
No, no, no, let go of that.

304
00:25:43,133 --> 00:25:46,222
Let go of that Kakoli!

305
00:26:06,519 --> 00:26:08,265
I have called the
police and their staff

306
00:26:08,495 --> 00:26:10,308
you gather the Bhaskar family.

307
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:12,120
Where are you going?

308
00:26:12,339 --> 00:26:13,796
Chief guest...

309
00:26:14,010 --> 00:26:15,337
to bring the Chief Ghost.

310
00:26:21,417 --> 00:26:23,261
A 150-year-old superstition.

311
00:26:24,815 --> 00:26:26,683
Ghosts and beasts.

312
00:26:27,698 --> 00:26:28,862
Skawndhokaata.

313
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:33,746
Half alive and half dead

314
00:26:33,827 --> 00:26:36,093
he would go straight for your head.

315
00:26:36,550 --> 00:26:39,756
Well, I have a story
that's a bit tragic.

316
00:26:39,897 --> 00:26:41,710
But it has varying degrees of pain.

317
00:26:42,558 --> 00:26:43,838
The first pain

318
00:26:44,265 --> 00:26:45,491
is a sweet pain.

319
00:26:45,706 --> 00:26:48,800
It's the pain of love,
complete with a background score.

320
00:26:51,847 --> 00:26:54,347
It's the pain of Bhaskar Villa's
Estate Manager Firdaus

321
00:26:55,019 --> 00:26:56,019
and Reena's pain.

322
00:26:57,592 --> 00:26:59,097
So? She liked him.

323
00:26:59,714 --> 00:27:00,827
It was a one-sided love.

324
00:27:01,361 --> 00:27:04,879
Once me and Ravi spoke to her,
Reena learnt her lesson.

325
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:07,680
Wrong answer.

326
00:27:07,737 --> 00:27:10,190
You didn't speak to her.
You forbid her.

327
00:27:10,231 --> 00:27:12,024
You scared and intimidated her.

328
00:27:12,878 --> 00:27:17,440
Well, Aunt Reena gathered her broken
heart and faded into the background

329
00:27:17,675 --> 00:27:20,474
and that is when a
new heroine entered.

330
00:27:20,498 --> 00:27:21,941
Why are you digging up dead bodies?

331
00:27:22,064 --> 00:27:23,283
Oh that reminds me!

332
00:27:25,626 --> 00:27:27,295
That was a brutal murder.

333
00:27:27,798 --> 00:27:30,361
Biren's murder by Skawndhokaata.

334
00:27:31,181 --> 00:27:32,399
You know Pakhi,

335
00:27:32,439 --> 00:27:36,134
Biren uncle was the
gardener at Bhaskar Villa.

336
00:27:37,001 --> 00:27:38,540
And Firdaus' roommate.

337
00:27:40,931 --> 00:27:42,551
And the other...

338
00:27:42,592 --> 00:27:43,791
Heroine, right?

339
00:27:45,236 --> 00:27:46,236
Swati.

340
00:27:48,751 --> 00:27:49,791
Swati Bhaskar.

341
00:27:51,830 --> 00:27:53,283
Sanjeev Bhaskar's wife.

342
00:27:53,336 --> 00:27:55,115
She was in an abusive marriage.

343
00:27:56,330 --> 00:27:57,719
Have you lost your mind?

344
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:59,673
Their pain was... the one with violins?

345
00:28:00,111 --> 00:28:01,717
Hemant, what is this nonsense?

346
00:28:01,840 --> 00:28:03,999
Why is he spewing lies
about your mother and I?

347
00:28:04,025 --> 00:28:05,025
Let him speak!

348
00:28:06,189 --> 00:28:07,189
Papa.

349
00:28:08,423 --> 00:28:11,595
So, Swati found
her love in Firdaus.

350
00:28:13,501 --> 00:28:14,541
But someone else

351
00:28:16,439 --> 00:28:17,509
saw their love.

352
00:28:19,337 --> 00:28:20,377
Right, Aunt Reena?

353
00:28:22,665 --> 00:28:23,853
I obeyed my brothers.

354
00:28:25,697 --> 00:28:26,994
I never stopped loving him.

355
00:28:27,556 --> 00:28:28,683
That's true.

356
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:32,478
That is why you told
your brothers everything.

357
00:28:33,486 --> 00:28:35,478
Ms. Reena told me...

358
00:28:36,439 --> 00:28:37,439
Firdaus...

359
00:28:38,181 --> 00:28:40,776
...the story of Firdaus and Swati.

360
00:28:41,063 --> 00:28:42,297
You know Ms. Reena,

361
00:28:43,384 --> 00:28:49,064
Swati and Firdaus had to
leave Daatganj because of you.

362
00:28:50,244 --> 00:28:53,689
But they returned to
Daatganj two years later.

363
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,320
Why did they return

364
00:28:55,354 --> 00:28:57,978
if they knew people
won't let them live here in peace?

365
00:28:58,240 --> 00:28:59,732
Because family is family.

366
00:29:00,564 --> 00:29:01,604
And a mother is a mother.

367
00:29:02,251 --> 00:29:04,080
She came back for her son Hemant.

368
00:29:10,806 --> 00:29:12,979
Then Aunt Reena
explained it to her brothers...

369
00:29:13,133 --> 00:29:14,879
that it's fine.
Two years have passed.

370
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:19,525
Forget it and forgive them.
But you didn't forget, did you?

371
00:29:20,433 --> 00:29:22,153
Fast-paced music plays here.

372
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:24,650
-To add some thrill.
-You have a son!

373
00:29:24,744 --> 00:29:26,683
Hey! Come with us! Come on!

374
00:29:26,724 --> 00:29:28,063
And Firdaus was killed.

375
00:29:31,173 --> 00:29:34,017
I am sure you all know who
the villain is by now.

376
00:29:34,572 --> 00:29:36,376
Then it is time

377
00:29:37,220 --> 00:29:38,583
for the vamp to enter.

378
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:40,400
Kakoli.

379
00:29:40,634 --> 00:29:43,154
Before she opened her shop with
Skawndhokaata's name

380
00:29:43,381 --> 00:29:44,714
she used to read horoscopes.

381
00:29:44,822 --> 00:29:46,509
Aunt Reena was her gold customer.

382
00:29:47,095 --> 00:29:49,822
Now the villain has to do
something to avoid the police.

383
00:29:51,173 --> 00:29:53,697
So they brought
Kakoli to their side.

384
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:57,430
You have to tell the villagers
that Skawndhokaata is back.

385
00:29:57,630 --> 00:29:58,763
Keep it.

386
00:29:59,837 --> 00:30:03,556
And that was how you
resurrected Skawndhokaata.

387
00:30:04,478 --> 00:30:07,080
You even won Biren
over to your side.

388
00:30:07,439 --> 00:30:09,986
And Biren told the villagers

389
00:30:10,345 --> 00:30:14,290
that he saw Firdaus running away
from Skawndhokaata.

390
00:30:16,361 --> 00:30:18,619
News confirmed and
the rumors spread.

391
00:30:19,939 --> 00:30:21,564
Firdaus was killed
by Skawndhokaata.

392
00:30:29,798 --> 00:30:32,220
You already know what
happened to your mother.

393
00:30:33,415 --> 00:30:36,415
Overdose of sleeping pills.
She committed suicide.

394
00:30:40,392 --> 00:30:41,712
So now the question is...

395
00:30:44,236 --> 00:30:49,698
who killed Biren,
Kakoli and Ravi uncle?

396
00:31:02,087 --> 00:31:03,807
Let’s ask Skwandhokata directly.

397
00:31:08,322 --> 00:31:09,362
Right Manoj?

398
00:31:16,408 --> 00:31:20,181
Manoj who became the Estate Manager
at such a young age.

399
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:26,040
You don't even have
hair on your face yet.

400
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,242
And you have already
committed three murders?

401
00:31:29,283 --> 00:31:30,997
You have killed more people right?

402
00:31:32,447 --> 00:31:34,392
Right? Before you joined here?

403
00:31:35,337 --> 00:31:36,377
Am I right Manoj?

404
00:31:37,103 --> 00:31:39,727
How many people have
you killed Manoj? Hey Manoj!

405
00:31:42,501 --> 00:31:44,962
You're a serial killer Manoj.

406
00:31:46,439 --> 00:31:47,853
Are you a serial killer Manoj?

407
00:31:50,595 --> 00:31:51,595
Jayavrat!

408
00:31:52,923 --> 00:31:55,896
Call the police and
take Manoj away.

409
00:31:56,043 --> 00:31:57,290
Not Manoj...

410
00:32:00,939 --> 00:32:01,939
Riyaz.

411
00:32:06,705 --> 00:32:07,821
Riyaz, the cleft on your upper lip,

412
00:32:07,845 --> 00:32:09,250
you have had that since
you were a child, right?

413
00:32:09,517 --> 00:32:11,376
I saw a picture of
you at Biren's house

414
00:32:11,869 --> 00:32:13,309
playing in Firdaus and Swati's lap.

415
00:32:14,197 --> 00:32:15,843
Cute kid...

416
00:32:15,950 --> 00:32:17,104
with a cleft.

417
00:32:18,439 --> 00:32:19,775
I wanted to tell you something,

418
00:32:21,001 --> 00:32:23,845
but don't tell anyone, okay?

419
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:26,150
Promise?

420
00:32:26,737 --> 00:32:27,850
Promise.

421
00:32:28,033 --> 00:32:29,033
Hemant...

422
00:32:30,814 --> 00:32:32,548
you have a younger brother now.

423
00:32:33,077 --> 00:32:34,090
Riyaz.

424
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,069
Look this is my son.

425
00:32:36,119 --> 00:32:39,830
Oh my God, you even had a son!

426
00:32:40,431 --> 00:32:42,189
He is with his aunt right now.

427
00:32:42,525 --> 00:32:44,251
I will introduce him to you soon.

428
00:32:44,978 --> 00:32:46,767
Mom passed away a few days later.

429
00:32:48,626 --> 00:32:50,017
But I didn't forget Riyaz.

430
00:32:52,103 --> 00:32:53,103
He was my brother.

431
00:32:56,751 --> 00:32:57,830
It took some time...

432
00:32:59,517 --> 00:33:00,557
but I found him.

433
00:33:12,025 --> 00:33:13,865
And then a few years
later I brought him here.

434
00:33:14,978 --> 00:33:16,103
With a new name.

435
00:33:18,587 --> 00:33:20,196
Riyaz hasn't killed anyone.

436
00:33:20,310 --> 00:33:22,043
This...

437
00:33:23,017 --> 00:33:25,783
is the spicy twist in this story.

438
00:33:28,220 --> 00:33:30,853
Radix pedis diaboli.

439
00:33:32,595 --> 00:33:33,595
Devil's foot.

440
00:33:35,376 --> 00:33:38,736
If anyone gets even
a whiff of its extract

441
00:33:40,330 --> 00:33:41,810
they lose their minds.

442
00:33:44,681 --> 00:33:45,673
And then

443
00:33:47,017 --> 00:33:50,825
every person or thing they see

444
00:33:51,845 --> 00:33:53,165
looks horrifying.

445
00:33:56,017 --> 00:33:57,737
And there is only one
way to end that fear.

446
00:33:59,673 --> 00:34:00,673
Suicide.

447
00:34:02,275 --> 00:34:04,450
That is what all of
Skawndhokaata's victims did.

448
00:34:07,298 --> 00:34:08,353
Suicide.

449
00:34:10,142 --> 00:34:11,142
I was going to do it too.

450
00:34:15,642 --> 00:34:16,642
Jayavrat saved me.

451
00:34:18,908 --> 00:34:20,603
Growing the devil's foot

452
00:34:22,650 --> 00:34:26,650
and removing its extract requires
a knowledge of botany.

453
00:34:29,689 --> 00:34:31,661
And only one person

454
00:34:32,696 --> 00:34:34,353
is that good at Botany here.

455
00:34:36,103 --> 00:34:37,103
Right Iraboty?

456
00:34:39,205 --> 00:34:41,962
The only thing Hemant is
passionate about is his plants.

457
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:44,251
He is a botany enthusiast.

458
00:34:45,814 --> 00:34:49,376
And this botany enthusiast
got the extract from the plant.

459
00:34:50,790 --> 00:34:54,931
Hemant knew when, how and where to
get his victims to smell the extract.

460
00:34:55,642 --> 00:34:58,095
Well, we already know

461
00:34:58,501 --> 00:35:01,978
who, how and why
Hemant killed them.

462
00:35:04,212 --> 00:35:05,236
We have the murderer,

463
00:35:07,408 --> 00:35:08,408
we have the motive,

464
00:35:09,939 --> 00:35:11,523
and we have the proof.

465
00:35:11,637 --> 00:35:12,737
Hemant?

466
00:35:12,947 --> 00:35:14,759
After Ravi, Biren and Kakoli...

467
00:35:17,009 --> 00:35:18,543
Was I next?

468
00:35:18,697 --> 00:35:20,150
Kakoli is still alive.

469
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:25,337
Ms. Reena and
Kakoli told us the truth

470
00:35:25,876 --> 00:35:28,189
and Kakoli is giving her
statement to the police.

471
00:35:30,509 --> 00:35:32,876
What you and Ravi
uncle did to our mother

472
00:35:33,845 --> 00:35:36,270
you deserve to be
punished for that.

473
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:39,240
Whether that might be going
to jail or dying by my hands.

474
00:35:40,283 --> 00:35:41,634
You are my father

475
00:35:42,970 --> 00:35:45,033
so I have made
arrangements for jail.

476
00:35:46,189 --> 00:35:48,189
I always knew the whole story.

477
00:35:49,033 --> 00:35:50,713
I just didn't have any
proof or witnesses.

478
00:35:51,853 --> 00:35:54,024
Unfortunately Kakoli survived but

479
00:35:54,892 --> 00:35:56,447
now she is ready to testify.

480
00:35:57,103 --> 00:35:59,822
Thanks to Mr. Home
and his investigation.

481
00:36:00,853 --> 00:36:02,361
And I hope that this will end

482
00:36:02,401 --> 00:36:05,649
the reign of Skawndhokaata’s terror
that spread out across Daatganj.

483
00:36:07,126 --> 00:36:08,126
Justice Chaudhary!

484
00:36:10,986 --> 00:36:11,986
Come in.

485
00:36:13,408 --> 00:36:16,626
You will find samples of Devil's
foot in Kakoli and Biren's blood.

486
00:36:18,165 --> 00:36:20,843
Tell the whole village
that Skawndhokaata

487
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:23,570
was just a game, that is now over.

488
00:36:33,275 --> 00:36:34,275
I am sorry.

489
00:36:35,447 --> 00:36:36,728
Was I too harsh?

490
00:36:39,408 --> 00:36:40,728
You have a good life young man.

491
00:36:42,978 --> 00:36:44,136
When is your train?

492
00:36:44,177 --> 00:36:45,317
In half an hour.

493
00:36:47,798 --> 00:36:50,298
Are you thinking that you made
a mistake by calling me here?

494
00:36:52,197 --> 00:36:54,590
I mean, they were
like a family to you

495
00:36:55,270 --> 00:36:56,670
and I sent them off to jail.

496
00:36:58,158 --> 00:37:00,744
Hemant wanted the truth to
come out and you helped him.

497
00:37:02,119 --> 00:37:04,003
I did not make a mistake
by calling you here.

498
00:37:04,063 --> 00:37:05,963
Well at least I have
one fixed client now.

499
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:10,556
You know, in the
future if there are any

500
00:37:12,048 --> 00:37:15,248
blackmails or murderers, even a
theft is fine, you know who to go to.

501
00:37:15,884 --> 00:37:16,884
-Shall we?
-Yeah.

502
00:37:17,603 --> 00:37:18,947
-Bye.
-Bye.

503
00:37:20,720 --> 00:37:21,720
Will we meet again?

504
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:40,376
Hi! Are you guys back?

505
00:37:40,908 --> 00:37:42,767
Yes, I will just go freshen up.

506
00:37:44,017 --> 00:37:45,712
You go too! Dirty...

507
00:37:58,533 --> 00:37:59,876
See you soon partner.

